[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6092281165","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346#issuecomment-6092281165","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124346","id":6092281165,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABayDVTQ","user":{"login":"014-code","id":161032298,"node_id":"U_kgDOCZkoag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161032298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code","html_url":"https://github.com/014-code","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-10T01:40:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T01:40:04Z","body":"**Fix Explanation**\r\n\r\nThe issue was found while moving nodes in the Scene Tree. Pressing `Ctrl + Up` or `Ctrl + Down` calls `SceneTreeDock::_tool_selected()`, which uses `Node::move_child()` to change the node order and then defers a call to `Tree::scroll_to_item()` to bring the moved node back into view.\r\n\r\nTracing the drawing code showed that sticky items are handled in `Tree::_notification(NOTIFICATION_DRAW)`. A parent item is fixed to the top of the Tree, and the content area is clipped below the sticky stack using `sticky_stack_end`.\r\n\r\nBefore this change, `scroll_to_item()` only accounted for the column title height:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\ny_offset -= title_button_height;\r\nscreen_h = area_size.height - title_button_height;\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt did not account for the space occupied by sticky items. As a result, the calculated visible area was larger than the actual usable area. The target node could end up underneath a sticky parent, while `scroll_to_item()` considered it visible and did not adjust the scroll position any further.\r\n\r\nThe existing `ensure_cursor_is_visible()` implementation already handled both cases correctly:\r\n\r\n- If the target item is sticky, use its `sticky_offset.y`.\r\n- For regular items, subtract the full `sticky_stack_end`.\r\n- Reduce the available viewport height by the sticky stack height.\r\n\r\nThe fix applies the same coordinate calculation to `scroll_to_item()`. The change is limited to `scene/gui/tree.cpp` around line 6621. No callers or sticky item rendering logic were changed. This fixes all existing users of `scroll_to_item()`, including the Scene Tree, Debugger Tree, Create Dialog, Inspector, and other editor Tree controls.\r\n\r\nThe FileSystem dock primarily uses `ensure_cursor_is_visible()`, which already includes the sticky item adjustment. The Skeleton3D joint tree explicitly disables sticky items, so neither requires an additional change.\r\n\r\nThe related tests passed locally.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6092281165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6113281718","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346#issuecomment-6113281718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124346","id":6113281718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbGFGtg","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-11T20:16:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T20:16:20Z","body":"Does not fix the problem in FileSystem dock:\r\n\r\n[Nagranie ekranu_20261011_221508.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/784c17b5-7b0a-4598-8afb-d62722b99627)\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6113281718/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6116851285","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346#issuecomment-6116851285","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124346","id":6116851285,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbJe-VQ","user":{"login":"014-code","id":161032298,"node_id":"U_kgDOCZkoag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161032298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code","html_url":"https://github.com/014-code","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T02:48:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T02:48:58Z","body":"> Does not fix the problem in FileSystem dock:\r\n> \r\n>  Nagranie.ekranu_20261011_221508.webm\r\n\r\nThanks for checking. You were right that the first version did not cover the FileSystem dock.\r\n\r\nThe FileSystem dock expands the parent folders and immediately calls `ensure_cursor_is_visible()`. Sticky item positions are rebuilt during the next Tree draw, so the immediate call could still use the previous sticky layout.\r\n\r\nI changed the FileSystem dock navigation and tree refresh paths to defer `ensure_cursor_is_visible()` until after the redraw. The existing `Tree::scroll_to_item()` fix remains in place for the Scene Tree and other Tree users.\r\n\r\nThe full PR checks now pass.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6116851285/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6123453396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346#issuecomment-6123453396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124346","id":6123453396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbPx71A","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T11:35:03Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T11:35:03Z","body":"> I changed the FileSystem dock navigation and tree refresh paths to defer ensure_cursor_is_visible() until after the redraw.\r\n\r\nThis didn't fix the problem. Did you even test it? 🤔","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6123453396/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6190561040","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346#issuecomment-6190561040","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124346","id":6190561040,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcPx3EA","user":{"login":"014-code","id":161032298,"node_id":"U_kgDOCZkoag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161032298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code","html_url":"https://github.com/014-code","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/014-code/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T11:04:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T13:38:17Z","body":"Thanks for calling this out, @KoBeWi and @AThousandShips. The FileSystem dock report was valid — the first fix only covered the immediate Tree scroll calculation.\r\n\r\nThe remaining issue was timing: the FileSystem dock asks the Tree to reveal the selected file before the sticky folder rows have been rebuilt during draw. `ensure_cursor_is_visible()` could therefore calculate against the old sticky layout and leave the file underneath the sticky row.\r\n\r\nI changed `Tree` to run the visibility calculation again after the sticky layout is applied. If the item is still outside the usable viewport, the correction stays queued for the next redraw. The FileSystem dock keeps using the deferred callback so the check happens after the tree update.\r\n\r\nI reproduced the FileSystem dock flow locally with a file near the bottom of the tree. `Show in FileSystem` now brings the file into view without an extra manual scroll.\r\n\r\nHere is the trimmed recording:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/014-code/godot/releases/download/pr-124346-filesystem-sticky-recording/PR-124346-filesystem-sticky-fixed.mp4","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6190561040/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused"